    },
    {
      "id": "M90mLm8bPxKvjG_9Io1TD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 949.25,
      "y": 2199.2734375,
      "width": 1008.579345703125,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#b2f2bb",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0K",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1724723035,
      "version": 440,
      "versionNonce": 848983963,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785224546946,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "RL - (formulate the problem statement into mathematical formulation - MDP - markov decision process)\n1. Dynamic programming - model based - dynamics of the enviroment model is known in advance\n2. Monte carlo - model free - dont need to model the environment dynamics before hand. \n3. SARSA - model free - Temporal Difference (0)\n4. TD (1..n)\n5. Policy gradient methods\n6. actor critic method\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "RL - (formulate the problem statement into mathematical formulation - MDP - markov decision process)\n1. Dynamic programming - model based - dynamics of the enviroment model is known in advance\n2. Monte carlo - model free - dont need to model the environment dynamics before hand. \n3. SARSA - model free - Temporal Difference (0)\n4. TD (1..n)\n5. Policy gradient methods\n6. actor critic method\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "RF7FDWsZnvR6Asjs7k5nO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 961.3671875,
      "y": 2474.91796875,
      "width": 787.0594482421875,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
